eservations</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Privacy</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Customer service</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Anthropic</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">OpenAI</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Google</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Meta</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">FAA</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">US</category><category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_des">Regulation and Deregulation</category><media:content url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/11/11/multimedia/11xp-ai-united-mpzg/11xp-ai-united-mpzg-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600.jpg" medium="image"><media:credit>Mike Blake/Reuters</media:credit><media:description>United Airlines moved to restrict A.I. agents’ access to customer accounts amid broader concerns about autonomous software that operates without human oversight.</media:description></media:content></item><item><title>Jensen Huang Resigns From Nvidia After Affairs</title><link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/nvidia-jensen-huang.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/nvidia-jensen-huang.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss</guid><atom:link rel="standout" href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/12/technology/nvidia-jensen-huang.html?partner=rss&amp;emc=rss" /><description>The chief executive has been under scrutiny for an affair with a woman said to be a Chinese spy, as well as for a relationship with a subordinate at his A.I. chip company. Nvidia’s finance chief, Colette Kress, was named interim leader.</description><dc:creator>Tripp Mickle and Maggie Haberman